{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 27, :comments ["<b>And the young man ran.</b> This is Gershom." "<b>And he told Moses.</b> Eldad and Medad were brothers of Moses, for when the Torah was given and the forbidden relations were prohibited, they all separated [from their wives], as it is said: ״וישמע משה את העם בכה למשפחותיו״, and we expound it as concerning the matter of their families. And also Amram, father of Moses, separated from Jochebed his wife and married another woman and begot from her Eldad and Medad. Eldad — 'El dod'; Medad — 'Mi dod', meaning 'challuf dod' [exchange of 'dod']. And I found a booklet from Rabbi Amram from Rabbi Hillel who was from the Land of Israel: 'I, Hillel, saw the grave of Eldad and Medad, and it was written on them: Eldad and Medad, brothers of Aaron from the father but not from the mother.' And some say: Eldad is Elidad son of Chislon; Medad is Kemuel son of Shaphan. And it was stated in Midrash Rabbi Tanchuma: because they humbled themselves, they merited to be superior to the elders in five things. The elders did not prophesy until the next day, as it is said: ״ואל העם תאמר התקדשו למחר״, but these prophesied what was destined to be at the end of forty years — they prophesied: 'Moses dies and Joshua brings Israel into the land.' And some say they prophesied concerning the downfall of Gog and Magog. The elders did not enter the land, but they — Elidad son of Chislon and Kemuel son of Shaphan — entered the land. The elders' names were not specified, but theirs were specified."], :book :numbers, :voice :daat-zkenim, :lang :en, :chapter 11, :notes {1 "Reading 'challuf dod' literally as 'exchange/interchange of dod' — possibly a wordplay or acrostic explanation; the text appears unvocalized and its precise meaning is uncertain."}, :source-witnesses [{"versionTitle" "Sefaria community Hebrew (PD)", "language" "he"}], :timestamp "2026-07-30T13:09:15.036080817Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}